Adaptation, not byte-identical upstream reproduction: retain Sculpt's explicit
pin mode, four-CSS-pixel click/drag tolerance, hit point/face normal, stored
camera position/controls target and numbered selectable HTML pin semantics.
Use the existing pinned Three.Raycaster and viewer scene/OrbitControls rather
than React Three Fiber/Drei or a second renderer. No vendor code is changed.
Unlike Sculpt's normalized world-space position, positions/normals here use
the current GLB/PLY scene root's local space; camera position/target retain the
existing viewer scene space. Root/world conversion uses Three matrices and
normal matrices, including non-uniform transforms. Focus restores that camera
snapshot immediately; it does not copy Sculpt's camera interpolation.
Static GLB mesh and PLY mesh/point annotations are supported. PLY Points
selection uses the vendored Three.js 0.186.1 Points.raycast implementation;
PerspectiveCamera.getViewSize converts a six-CSS-pixel interaction tolerance
into a world-space threshold. The adapter stores geometry position[hit.index],
transformed through the point object's matrixWorld into root-local coordinates,
not Three's closest point on the picking ray. Point clouds do not invent face
normals or opaque surfaces: pins are projected without per-frame point-buffer
occlusion scans, while actual meshes retain the existing raycast occlusion.
SKP picking and tracking anchors across asset replacement, animation, skinning
or morphs are not claimed.
The application binds asset revision and prefilters private/public marker access.
